        "evidence": "topological-mass-cat-transient-proof.md:16-17 'the norm of the sum equals the sum of the norms (by disjointness of the supports)'",
        "notes": "The claim ‖Σ_i tr_trans(ϱ,p_i)‖ = Σ_i ‖tr_trans(ϱ,p_i)‖ from 'disjointness of supports' is generally FALSE for a Killing-form (Euclidean-type) norm: orthogonal/disjoint summands give the Pythagorean ‖Σ x_i‖² = Σ‖x_i‖² (an L2 sum), not the linear L1 sum ‖Σ x_i‖ = Σ‖x_i‖. Disjoint supports never upgrade an L2-orthogonality to L1-additivity. The triangle inequality gives ≤, equality requires colinearity, not disjointness. Flagged warn (not critical) because the norm convention is not pinned and the parent lemma's normed claim is the load-bearing one."
